<title>USA: Rolls-Royce-Powered Boeing 777 Earns ETOPS okay.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce-Powered Boeing 777 Earns ETOPS okay.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co on Thursday said the U.S. Federal Aviation Administration granted extended-range twin-engine operations (ETOPS) approval to Boeing 777 airliners powered by Rolls-Royce Plc Trent 800 engines.</p>
<p>FAA type design approval acknowledges that the engine/aircraft design is reliable for ETOPS qualification. This allows twin-engine aircraft to fly long-distance routes, many over water, up to 180 minutes flying time from primary and alternate airports.</p>
</text>
